              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "seanbean1"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this for a school project with homegrown chiles and tomatoes. We only had bell peppers and jalapenos and dried cilantro but it turned out great."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "djsyn66"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great salsa. Made it a few times. Instead of using a grill I use my pellet smoker with mesquite pellets. Smoke all the tomatoes, peppers and onion on HiSmoke (225F) for about 1h30 to 2h. No need for the liquid smoke!",
            "datePublished": "2019-12-22T01:38:09.837Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Gina Gonzalez"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Extremely good. Thank you for your tip to cover the peppers to let them steam while they cool to make them easier to peel. Can be modified to suit your needs. I just had poblano and red bell peppers used all of the other ingredients except the liquid smoke and added a 1/2 tsp sugar. I left the salsa chunky. Sauteed with shrimp and served over pan steamed tilapia. It was great!",
            "datePublished": "2015-07-08T07:34:15.747Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Added more jalapeño and used apple cider vinegar. Also, used hickory smoke because that’s what I had. Good recipe. I’m sure it was fine the way it was created.",
            "datePublished": "2024-03-29T13:54:34.379Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Amber Roeder"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Yummy, I thought it made waaaay too much... and four days later I need to make more.\nMake sure you really blister the peppers, or else it is hard to skin them. (Not the end of the world if the skin is on, just more texture)\nI did triple the garlic, because that's what I do with every recipe. Other than that - perfect!",
            "datePublished": "2016-08-13T18:20:37.173Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Banfrau"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Wow, this is the recipe I have been looking for. I wasn't able to get the poblano peppers, so I used 4 jalapeno, and it is good and spicy the way I like it. I've tried many recipes for salsa on this site, and while I do like most, they all start with canned tomatoes. This tends to make most of them taste overall the same. The hardest part was peeling the peppers, and even though it didn't bother me, I will experiment with uncooked peppers next time just because I love fresh peppers.",
            "datePublished": "2015-07-22T10:48:48.303Z"
          },
          {
